{"id":"8bbd77b21a9519f1","group":"93","path":"93/93-df-maximal-theory.md","title":"Maximal Theory","display":"df-maximal-theory — Maximal Theory","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Algebraizable Logics","book_abbrev":"93","label":"93-df-maximal-theory","aliases":["93-df-maximal-theory"],"display":"df-maximal-theory — Maximal Theory","depends_on":["[[93-df-consistency]]","[[93-df-logic]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"93"},{"key":"label","html":"93-df-maximal-theory"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>93-df-maximal-theory</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-maximal-theory — Maximal Theory"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"959f67178eec388a\" href=\"?note=959f67178eec388a\" title=\"93-df-consistency\">93-df-consistency</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"bd7e4207897c8db3\" href=\"?note=bd7e4207897c8db3\" title=\"93-df-logic\">93-df-logic</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal L\">\\(\\mathcal L\\)</span> is a candidate pair <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\langle F,\\vdash_{\\mathcal L}\\rangle\">\\(\\langle F,\\vdash_{\\mathcal L}\\rangle\\)</span>; its components are bound in the assertion.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}\\)</span> is the nontriviality predicate of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"959f67178eec388a\" href=\"?note=959f67178eec388a\" title=\"93-df-consistency\">93-df-consistency</a>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MaxTh}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{MaxTh}_{93}\\)</span> is defined here.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}maximal\\text{-}theory}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{MaxTh}_{93}(T,\\mathcal L)\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists F\\;\\exists\\vdash_{\\mathcal L}\\;\\Bigl[{}&amp;\n\\mathcal L=\\langle F,\\vdash_{\\mathcal L}\\rangle\n\\land\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}(T,\\mathcal L)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall\\varphi\\in F\\;(T\\vdash_{\\mathcal L}\\varphi\\to\\varphi\\in T)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall U\\subseteq F\\;\\Bigl(\nT\\subsetneq U\n\\land\\forall\\varphi\\in F\\;(U\\vdash_{\\mathcal L}\\varphi\\to\\varphi\\in U)\n\\to\\neg\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}(U,\\mathcal L)\\Bigr)\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}maximal\\text{-}theory}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{MaxTh}_{93}(T,\\mathcal L)\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists F\\;\\exists\\vdash_{\\mathcal L}\\;\\Bigl[{}&amp;\n\\mathcal L=\\langle F,\\vdash_{\\mathcal L}\\rangle\n\\land\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}(T,\\mathcal L)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall\\varphi\\in F\\;(T\\vdash_{\\mathcal L}\\varphi\\to\\varphi\\in T)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall U\\subseteq F\\;\\Bigl(\nT\\subsetneq U\n\\land\\forall\\varphi\\in F\\;(U\\vdash_{\\mathcal L}\\varphi\\to\\varphi\\in U)\n\\to\\neg\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}(U,\\mathcal L)\\Bigr)\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Both closure and maximality use the consequence relation recovered from the displayed logic pair. The quantified competitor is a strictly larger closed set in the same formula universe, so no ambient <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F\">\\(F\\)</span> or induced operator is hidden.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"93-df-consistency","status":"resolved","id":"959f67178eec388a","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-consistency]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-logic","status":"resolved","id":"bd7e4207897c8db3","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-logic]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-consistency","status":"resolved","id":"959f67178eec388a","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}$ is the nontriviality predicate of [[93-df-consistency]], and $\\mathrm{MaxTh}_{93}$ is defined here.","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathcal L","display":false},{"tex":"\\langle F,\\vdash_{\\mathcal L}\\rangle","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{MaxTh}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}maximal\\text{-}theory}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{MaxTh}_{93}(T,\\mathcal L)\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists F\\;\\exists\\vdash_{\\mathcal L}\\;\\Bigl[{}&\n\\mathcal L=\\langle F,\\vdash_{\\mathcal L}\\rangle\n\\land\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}(T,\\mathcal L)\\\\\n&\\land\\forall\\varphi\\in F\\;(T\\vdash_{\\mathcal L}\\varphi\\to\\varphi\\in T)\\\\\n&\\land\\forall U\\subseteq F\\;\\Bigl(\nT\\subsetneq U\n\\land\\forall\\varphi\\in F\\;(U\\vdash_{\\mathcal L}\\varphi\\to\\varphi\\in U)\n\\to\\neg\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}(U,\\mathcal L)\\Bigr)\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"F","display":false}],"bytes":1324,"backlinks":[{"id":"dc3498f98607795c","anchor":"ref-10","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{MaxTh}_{93}$, $\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}$, and $\\mathrm{CompleteTh}_{93}$ are the predicates of [[93-df-maximal-theory]], [[93-df-consistency]], and [[93-df-complete-theory]]."},{"id":"def48430496c026c","anchor":"ref-8","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{MaxTh}_{93}$ is the maximal-consistent-theory predicate of [[93-df-maximal-theory]]."},{"id":"882ddfff5f1c7a82","anchor":"ref-8","locations":["元数